    <string name="onboarding_1_title">A dungeon made of words</string>
    <string name="onboarding_1_body">This is a vocabulary game wearing a dungeon.\n\nEvery monster is a set of word puzzles, every fight is a study session, and the words are the point. The dungeon is just what makes you come back.\n\nA spaced-repetition scheduler decides which words you meet, disguised as difficulty.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_2_title">The descent</string>
    <string name="onboarding_2_body">Three floors, four steps each. At every step you pick one of two nodes: a battle, a rest, a treasure, an elite, or the boss at the end of floor three.\n\nHP carries across floors. There is no free heal between them.\n\nAnd the important part: dying never takes back what you learned. Your word progress is untouchable. A lost run costs you the run, nothing else — words you missed simply come back sooner.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_3_title">Combat</string>
    <string name="onboarding_3_body">Monsters have no health bar. They have question slots — answer them all and the monster is gone.\n\nDamage runs backwards from what you would expect: missing an easy word hurts most, and missing a word above your level barely stings. That is on purpose, so reaching above your level is never a death sentence.\n\nThe timer only ever helps you. Answering fast reduces damage; answering slowly never adds any.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_4_title">Reading the grid</string>
    <string name="onboarding_4_body">Some puzzles give letter-by-letter feedback:\n\n  ✓ right letter, right place\n  ~ right letter, wrong place\n  ✗ not in the word\n\nEvery colour on screen is paired with a glyph like these, so nothing depends on telling green from yellow.\n\nStart at Practice for a quiet review session, or Realm Select to descend.</string>

